---
layout: base.njk
title: Mods — Thurbox
description: Official and community mods for Thurbox, discovered from the thurbox-mods GitHub topic.
extraCss: [gallery.css]
activeNav: mods
footer: true
navScrolled: true
---
{% import "gallery.njk" as gallery %}
<div class="container plugin-page">
  <header class="plugin-intro">
    <p class="plugin-eyebrow">Extend your workspace</p>
    <h1>Mods</h1>
    <p>Panes, extensions and themes published on GitHub, discovered automatically from the <a href="https://github.com/topics/thurbox-mods"><code>thurbox-mods</code></a> topic. Install one with its command, then follow its README for setup.</p>
    <p><a href="#submit-mod">Publish yours</a> · <a href="./docs/interface.html">Mod guide</a> · Looking for new resource kinds? See <a href="./fleet-plugins.html">Fleet plugins</a>.</p>
  </header>
  <p class="plugin-notice">Official mods are maintained by Thurbeen. Community mods list themselves with the topic and are not reviewed by Thurbeen: read the README and check the capability grants a mod asks for before you install it.</p>
  {{ gallery.controls(modGallery, "mods", "Name, owner, topic or description") }}
  <div class="plugin-grid" id="plugin-grid">
    {% for mod in modGallery %}{{ gallery.card(mod) }}{% endfor %}
  </div>
  <p id="plugin-empty" hidden>No mods match these filters. Try another search or reset the filters.</p>
  <section class="plugin-submit" id="submit-mod" aria-labelledby="submit-heading">
    <h2 id="submit-heading">Publish your mod</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>Publish the mod in a public GitHub repository.</li>
      <li>Add the <a href="https://github.com/topics/thurbox-mods"><code>thurbox-mods</code></a> topic to the repository.</li>
      <li>Optional: put a screenshot or GIF at <code>media/demo.gif</code>, or describe the listing in your <code>mod.toml</code>, as below.</li>
    </ol>
    <p>The site rebuilds every day. It reads each repository’s name, owner, description, stars, last push and topics from GitHub, and its version and required Thurbox version from <code>mod.toml</code>. Forks and archived repositories are left out. No pull request and no review queue.</p>
    <pre data-title="mod.toml"><code class="language-toml">[gallery]
media = "media/demo.gif"
media_alt = "What the screenshot shows"
platforms = ["Linux", "macOS"]
notes = "Required capability grants, layout changes and conflicts."</code></pre>
    <p>Every field is optional. <code>media</code> is a path in the repository or an HTTPS URL. The install command is <code>thurbox-cli mod install git+</code> and the repository URL. A mod that needs another command asks for it in the reviewed overlay. The <a href="https://github.com/Thurbeen/thurbox/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md#mod-gallery">contributing guide</a> describes the curated overlay that maintainers use for notes and removals.</p>
    <details><summary>Official repositories outside this gallery</summary><p><a href="https://github.com/Thurbeen/thurbox-plugin-orchestrator">thurbox-plugin-orchestrator</a> is archived and targets the earlier admin plugin model. <a href="https://github.com/Thurbeen/thurbox-discord">thurbox-discord</a> manages the community Discord server; it is not a Thurbox add-on.</p></details>
  </section>
</div>
<script src="./js/gallery.js"></script>
